screen.SHADOWS=Shadows
screen.LIGHTING=Lighting

profile.comment=POTATO runs on anything. LOW is playable on integrated graphics. MEDIUM targets 60fps at 12 chunks on midrange hardware. HIGH is for headroom to spare.

# ---- Shadows ---------------------------------------------------------------
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Size of the shadow map, in pixels per side. The single biggest shadow quality/cost lever. 2048 is the sensible default; 4096 quadruples the memory and fill cost.

option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far from you shadows are drawn, in blocks. Raising this spreads the same number of shadow texels over more world, so distant shadows get softer AND nearer ones get blockier. Raise the resolution with it.
suffix.shadowDistance= blocks

option.SHADOW_QUALITY=Shadow Filter
option.SHADOW_QUALITY.comment=How many taps the soft-shadow filter takes. Off gives hard, aliased edges but is nearly free.
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.0=Hard
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.1=Soft
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.2=Softest

option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Width of the soft shadow edge, in shadow texels. Costs nothing extra, but too wide and shadows start leaking through thin walls.

option.SHADOW_BIAS_SCALE=Shadow Bias
option.SHADOW_BIAS_SCALE.comment=Normal-offset bias strength. Raise it if you see shimmering stripes on lit surfaces (shadow acne). Lower it if shadows look detached from whatever is casting them.

option.SHADOW_DISTORTION=Shadow Focus
option.SHADOW_DISTORTION.comment=Concentrates shadow map texels near you, where you can actually see the detail, at the cost of distant shadow sharpness. 0 spreads them evenly.

# ---- Lighting --------------------------------------------------------------
option.SUNLIGHT_STRENGTH=Sunlight
option.SUNLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of direct light from the sun and moon.

option.SKYLIGHT_STRENGTH=Skylight
option.SKYLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of ambient light from the sky. This is what fills in shadowed areas outdoors.

option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of light from torches, lava and other light-emitting blocks.

option.SSAO=Ambient Occlusion
option.SSAO.comment=Darkens creases and corners where light has trouble reaching. Applied to ambient light only, so it never dirties surfaces the sun is hitting directly.

option.SSAO_QUALITY=AO Samples
option.SSAO_QUALITY.comment=How many neighbours each pixel tests. More is smoother and slower.
value.SSAO_QUALITY.0=Low
value.SSAO_QUALITY.1=Medium
value.SSAO_QUALITY.2=High

option.SSAO_STRENGTH=AO Strength
option.SSAO_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the occlusion gets.

option.SSAO_RADIUS=AO Radius
option.SSAO_RADIUS.comment=How far, in blocks, a surface looks for things occluding it. Larger radii catch bigger features but sample more sparsely.
suffix.SSAO_RADIUS= blocks

screen.WATER=Water

option.WATER_WAVES=Waves
option.WATER_WAVES.comment=Displaces the water surface with three travelling waves. The surface normal is the exact derivative of that displacement, so highlights sit on the crests instead of sliding around.

option.WAVE_STRENGTH=Wave Height
option.WAVE_STRENGTH.comment=How tall the waves are. Water is a flat quad at the top of its block, so very tall waves will poke into the block above.

option.WAVE_SPEED=Wave Speed
option.WAVE_SPEED.comment=How fast the waves travel.

option.WATER_NORMAL_STRENGTH=Ripple Detail
option.WATER_NORMAL_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the surface normal relative to the actual displacement. Above 1 this adds ripple detail finer than the block-corner vertex grid could ever represent. Costs nothing.

option.SSR=Reflections
option.SSR.comment=Screen-space reflections on water. Only reflects what is already on screen; anything else falls back to the sky colour.

option.SSR_QUALITY=Reflection Quality
option.SSR_QUALITY.comment=How many steps each reflection ray takes. Low can miss thin or distant geometry and fall back to sky.
value.SSR_QUALITY.0=Low
value.SSR_QUALITY.1=Medium
value.SSR_QUALITY.2=High

option.WATER_ABSORPTION=Water Clarity
option.WATER_ABSORPTION.comment=How fast light is absorbed with depth. Higher means shallow water stays clear but deep water goes dark blue-green sooner. 0 makes water completely clear.

option.WATER_REFRACTION=Refraction
option.WATER_REFRACTION.comment=Bends what you see through the water surface, following the waves.

option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Caustics
option.WATER_CAUSTICS.comment=The rippling bands of focused light on surfaces underwater.

screen.SKY=Sky & Clouds

option.CUSTOM_SKY=Analytic Sky
option.CUSTOM_SKY.comment=Replaces vanilla's sky texture with a gradient computed from the sun's position, including the glow around the sun. Off falls back to vanilla's sky colours.

option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS=Volumetric Clouds
option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS.comment=Replaces vanilla's flat cloud layer with a raymarched one. This is the most expensive option in the pack and the first thing to turn off if the framerate is short. Off restores vanilla clouds.

option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Cloud Steps
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=How many samples each cloud ray takes. This is the direct cost/quality dial: fewer steps means softer, blurrier clouds and a much cheaper frame.
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.0=Low
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.1=Medium
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.2=High
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.3=Ultra

option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=How much of the sky the clouds fill.

option.CLOUD_HEIGHT=Cloud Altitude
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment=Height of the cloud layer. Clouds are drawn in the sky pass, so standing above this height means they will not be drawn over the terrain below you.
suffix.CLOUD_HEIGHT= blocks

option.CLOUD_SPEED=Cloud Speed
option.CLOUD_SPEED.comment=How fast clouds drift on the wind.

screen.POST=Post Processing

option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment=Glow around bright things, built from a downsample/upsample mip chain rather than one wide blur, so the falloff is smooth and wide without being expensive.

option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom Strength
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the glow is mixed into the image.

option.AUTO_EXPOSURE=Auto Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=Adapts overall brightness to the scene, like an eye. Walking out of a cave into daylight will briefly look too bright, then settle.

option.EXPOSURE=Exposure
option.EXPOSURE.comment=Manual brightness multiplier, applied on top of auto exposure.

option.EXPOSURE_SPEED=Adaptation Speed
option.EXPOSURE_SPEED.comment=How fast auto exposure settles. Darkening is always faster than brightening, the way eyes actually work.

option.TONEMAP=Tonemap
option.TONEMAP.comment=The curve that maps HDR light onto your display. Uchimura keeps mid-tone contrast through a linear section; ACES is punchier and more saturated. None simply clips, which blows out highlights.
value.TONEMAP.0=None
value.TONEMAP.1=Uchimura
value.TONEMAP.2=ACES

option.VIGNETTE=Vignette
option.VIGNETTE.comment=Slight darkening toward the corners.

option.VIGNETTE_STRENGTH=Vignette Strength
option.VIGNETTE_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the corners get.

screen.COLOR=Colour

option.COLOR_GRADING=Colour Grading
option.COLOR_GRADING.comment=Master switch for saturation, vibrance, contrast and white balance. Off gives you the raw tonemapped image.

option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.SATURATION.comment=Overall colour intensity. 1.0 leaves the image untouched. Applied around perceived brightness, so raising it does not shift hues.

option.VIBRANCE=Vibrance
option.VIBRANCE.comment=Boosts dull colours much more than already-vivid ones. This is the dial to raise if the world looks drab: it lifts muted greens and browns without driving lava and sunsets into neon.

option.CONTRAST=Contrast
option.CONTRAST.comment=Contrast about mid-grey. Small changes go a long way; above about 1.15 shadows start clipping to black.

option.WHITE_BALANCE=Warmth
option.WHITE_BALANCE.comment=Colour temperature. Positive is warmer and more golden, negative is cooler and bluer. Applied in linear light before the tonemap, the way a camera does it, and luminance-preserving so it tints without changing brightness.
